  "story": "A festival has one stage. Each band asks for the stage from a start minute to an end minute and would draw a crowd of a known size; the requests are listed by end minute, earliest first. Two bands cannot play at the same time, but one may start in the very minute another ends. Choose the bands so that the total crowd is as large as possible, and report that total. An early slot is not always worth taking: one long concert with a huge crowd can beat several small ones.",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "starts", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "ends", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "crowd", "type": "array<num>"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 0, "max": 300},
    "notes": ["0 to 300 requests; the three lists have the same length.", "Minutes are whole numbers from 0 to 2000 and a request ends after it starts.", "Crowds are whole numbers from 1 to 500."]
  },
  "blocks": {
    "allow": ["arith.add", "arith.floor_div", "arith.max", "arith.sub", "arr.append", "arr.get", "arr.len", "arr.set", "cmp.ge", "cmp.le", "cmp.lt", "ctrl.else", "ctrl.for_range", "ctrl.if", "ctrl.return", "ctrl.while", "lit.num", "logic.and", "new.array", "var.get", "var.set"],
    "maxBlocks": 90
  },
  "limits": {"maxOps": 600000, "maxDepth": 32, "maxAlloc": 5000},
  "hints": ["Answer the question for the first 1, 2, 3 … requests in turn and keep the answers in a list that starts with 0.", "Request i is either left out, and the answer stays what it was, or taken: then add its crowd to the best answer for the requests that end no later than it starts. Keep the MAX of the two.", "The requests are sorted by end minute, so the ones that end in time are a beginning of the list. Find how many they are, by stepping back or by halving with FLOOR DIVIDE, and use that count as the position in your list of answers."],
  "validators": {"output": "equal"},
